3,102,22],[25921,23.2,2012,49,100,22],[25922,23.4,2012,47,103,20],[25923,23.7,2012,48,111,24],[25924,24.0,2012,49,117,27]],"links":[["Custer County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/nebraska/custer-county"],["ARC or PLC in Custer County","/arc-plc/nebraska/custer-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Custer County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 17 grids, November to December came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, that same middle saw May to June at 137% and June to July at 148%, but November to December fell to 39%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 18% of normal on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
